✓ Plan generated

⚠  requires_human = true  A human must review this plan before code generation 
proceeds.

Goal
Fix the `CONSOLE_HTML_FORMAT` template in the Rich console so the `<html>` tag 
wraps `<head>` and `<body>`, making `export_html()` produce valid HTML.

Files to modify
  • rich/console.py

Implementation steps
  1. Step 1: In `rich/console.py`, locate the module-level string constant 
`CONSOLE_HTML_FORMAT`.
  2. Step 2: Modify `CONSOLE_HTML_FORMAT` by moving the `<html>` opening tag 
(and any attributes) to the position immediately before the `<head>` opening 
tag, ensuring the `</html>` closing tag remains after the `</body>` closing tag.
For example, if the template currently contains `<head>...</head>\n<html>`, 
change it to `<html>\n<head>...</head>`.

Tests to run
  $ pytest tests/test_console.py -k html

Risks
  ⚠  If other code or tests do brittle string matching on the exact whitespace 
or tag order of `export_html()` output, they may need minor updates.

